WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.833
Let's build the RNA one base at

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:02.356
a time.

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:04.573
Here's a T on the template strand.

00:00:05.107 --> 00:00:06.443
The RNA gets an A.

00:00:06.895 --> 00:00:08.114
Next, a C.

00:00:08.509 --> 00:00:09.902
The RNA gets a G.

00:00:10.355 --> 00:00:11.969
Then a G, so the RNA gets

00:00:12.004 --> 00:00:12.515
a C.

00:00:13.142 --> 00:00:14.988
Every new RNA base pairs with the

00:00:15.034 --> 00:00:15.893
template strand.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.331
None pair with the coding strand.

00:00:18.958 --> 00:00:20.827
Like matching a pattern, piece by piece.

00:00:21.361 --> 00:00:22.813
So the template strand is the one

00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:23.184
read.

00:00:23.718 --> 00:00:25.088
Now try the question again.
